Beasts who inspire fear through reckless consumption. Think Frank Booth from Blue Velvet, or the Macellarius Bloodline from Vampire: The Requiem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T17:06:47-07:00","id":858611,"title":"","content":"Hungers aren't Familes,Espirit. Anakim, Makara, Ugallu, not the Tyrants, the Ravagers, or the Nemesis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T19:21:50-07:00","id":858677,"title":"","content":"Some months ago I made a family based on the losing you senses! with aa birthright and sample atavism!<br /> me and some people from the forum dioscussed it here; <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/656667-i-made-a-homebrew-family\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/656667-i-made-a-homebrew-family\"> I Made a Homebrew Family :&gt; - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/656667-i-made-a-homebrew-family\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/656667-i-made-a-homebrew-family </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Hello Dudes and Dudettes and people who don't fit in the gender binary. i was thinking to myself,Beast has the potential to have more splats,cause people have been havijng nightmares since the dawn of mankind,and there kinds of nightmares that were not explored in the game so here my take on one of them! </div> </div> </div><br /> And here's the write-up!<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1v-7uNxTuOVEyMJ0ixmvYfWoPZysOkLM0GJU915g-67Q/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...915g-67Q/edit#</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 04-03-2016, 10:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T19:47:13-07:00","id":858688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/858600-missing-families-hungers?p=858611#post858611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hungers aren't Familes,Espirit. Anakim, Makara, Ugallu, not the Tyrants, the Ravagers, or the Nemesis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. I am aware. I. . . think there's been some sort of miscommunication here. I wasn't certain about new Families so I was answering the part of Matt's query where he asked about Hungers.<br /> <br /> Or are you saying that hedonism is better suited as a Family than a Hunger?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T19:56:06-07:00","id":858693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/858600-missing-families-hungers?p=858688#post858688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes. I am aware. I. . . think there's been some sort of miscommunication here. I wasn't certain about new Families so I was answering the part of Matt's query where he asked about Hungers.<br /> <br /> Or are you saying that hedonism is better suited as a Family than a Hunger?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, no, sorry, I made a dumb, dumb mistake. I originally thought this was only Families, not Hunger. Turns out, it's both.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> My bad, I missed details in haste! Forgive me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T20:08:57-07:00","id":858707,"title":"","content":"Heh, it's all good. I was incredibly confused for a moment, is all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T20:16:44-07:00","id":858715,"title":"","content":"How about time and age or something akin to change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T20:19:14-07:00","id":858718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/858600-missing-families-hungers?p=858610#post858610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there may be space for a Hunger for Pleasure or Excess, wanton hedonist Beasts who inspire fear through reckless consumption. Think Frank Booth from Blue Velvet, or the Macellarius Bloodline from Vampire: The Requiem.</div> </div> </div> </div> Sorry to say, but such a Hunger could be tied to Predators (thrill of the chase, be it in dark woods or crime investigations), Collectors (the pride of convincing anyone to become your lover/retainer, the joy of taking sensual relics worth millions), and if you want to get really dark, Tyrants (you all exist only to satisfy my whims, or else).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T20:37:10-07:00","id":858732,"title":"","content":"Would fear of isolation be a viable option for families? I mean I'm not sure it might mesh in with other families, but the only one I can think of is that it might fit in with exposure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T20:57:36-07:00","id":858743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/858600-missing-families-hungers?p=858732#post858732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would fear of isolation be a viable option for families? I mean I'm not sure it might mesh in with other families, but the only one I can think of is that it might fit in with exposure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eshmaki already cover that one rather directly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T21:29:54-07:00","id":858761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/858600-missing-families-hungers?p=858732#post858732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would fear of isolation be a viable option for families? I mean I'm not sure it might mesh in with other families, but the only one I can think of is that it might fit in with exposure.</div> </div> </div> </div> I agree with Satchel. Also, &quot;Exposure&quot; is the exact word used to describe the fear embodied by the Ugallu.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T00:01:47-07:00","id":858800,"title":"","content":"How about &quot;nightmares of shame&quot; for a family? Or guilt? Or is that too close to a Hunger, and thus Nemeses?<br /> <br /> (Edit: Actually, it might just fall under Anakim or Namtaru, or even Ugallu.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 04-04-2016, 03:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T00:05:47-07:00","id":858802,"title":"","content":"Isn't a nightmare of shame Exposure?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T01:14:04-07:00","id":858824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baroqo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/858600-missing-families-hungers?p=858608#post858608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about a <b>&quot;fear of self&quot; </b>family?<br /> <br /> Makaras could do for it, but i think that - expanded enough - they could make a nice addition.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would think Gorgons over Leviathans there.<br /> <br /> What type of monsters do you imagine drawing from that fear?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T01:14:39-07:00","id":858825,"title":"","content":"Fear of failure maybe. Examples could be a sphynx - fail my riddle and I'll eat you. Ammit from Egyptian mythology; and any myth where only those of the correct moral charachter can pass really.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T01:27:54-07:00","id":858830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/858600-missing-families-hungers?p=858802#post858802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't a nightmare of shame Exposure?</div> </div> </div> </div>As above, that's pretty much what I came to just as you posted. I guess you could argue that shame (or at least guilt) is often internal, whereas Ugallu externalise things, but it's probably too fine a hair to split, and exposing someone to guilt them is pretty much just Ugallu/Nemesis. Not to mention guilt as a form of hopelessness, or as a form of (self)-revulsion, etc.<br /> <br /> I argued myself out of this one hours ago anyway, heh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 04-04-2016, 04:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T03:05:09-07:00","id":858851,"title":"","content":"I went through a few lists of fears in search of something new. It's harder than I expected. A lot of fears could be covered by existing Families/Hungers, if you consider their implications broadly. That's why, even if we fail to find anything new, a few paragraphs in the Player's Guide to broaden these concepts wouldn't hurt. Most notably:<br /> <br /> Deceit/Revelation. As of now, the description of Makara focuses on aquatic themes. This makes them stand out among other families, who are often closer to ideas that environments. However, the general feeling I get from the Forums is that they are THE family for all the deceptive or enticing monsters (like Gumiho or Succubi), regardless of surroundings. The fear would stem from the revelation that you made bad choices or put your guard down and played along to your doom. If Makara need to focus on aquatic themes, this could be basis for another Family.<br /> <br /> Actually, lies and deceit could be basis for another Hunger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T03:17:47-07:00","id":858857,"title":"","content":"Hunger of Twist?<br /> The idea is based upon the character of Joker (Nolan version).<br /> The beast seek to scramble the life of the victim up down.<br /> It is not simply prey or collector (it must not &quot;tag&quot; a victim or stole/harm, anyting), or Nemesis (a routine is not a &quot;wrong&quot; about nobody, per se), neither ruin (the subject is a single person and the change is not only about &quot;damage&quot;).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T05:25:57-07:00","id":858907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Throne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/858600-missing-families-hungers?p=858857#post858857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hunger of Twist?<br /> The idea is based upon the character of Joker (Nolan version).<br /> The beast seek to scramble the life of the victim up down.<br /> It is not simply prey or collector (it must not &amp;quot;tag&amp;quot; a victim or stole/harm, anyting), or Nemesis (a routine is not a &amp;quot;wrong&amp;quot; about nobody, per se), neither ruin (the subject is a single person and the change is not only about &amp;quot;damage&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see that working. Hunger for Change working in direct opposition to the Nemesis hunger for Order.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T05:39:23-07:00","id":858912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/858600-missing-families-hungers?p=858907#post858907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see that working. Hunger for Change working in direct opposition to the Nemesis hunger for Order.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that would come under Ruin.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T06:34:45-07:00","id":858953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/858600-missing-families-hungers?p=858610#post858610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there may be space for a Hunger for Pleasure or Excess, wanton hedonist Beasts who inspire fear through reckless consumption. Think Frank Booth from Blue Velvet, or the Macellarius Bloodline from Vampire: The Requiem.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Hunger for Pleasure is one that I would really like to see. If it doesn't make it into the Player's Guide, I might just have to homebrew it. While I can see some overlap with some of the others that GibberingEloquence mentioned, I can also see some overlap between the existing Hungers, as well. The key difference that I'd see is that seeking excess might not be directly harmful by default, nor would it necessarily mean taking something from someone else. Although I suppose that, to be fair, I've never really seen how taking a new lover for one's Hoard necessarily constitutes a loss on the side of said lover. <br /> <br /> I would like to see a Hunger for Secrets as well. I see this as different from the Hoard in that a secret doesn't need to be taken from someone else necessarily. I'd imagine that the power of a secret, and thus how satisfying it would be to the Horror, would depend both on the obscurity of the knowledge gained and its potential effect should it be revealed. This would mean that learning that a gardener has created a new bloom for the next flower show would be a pretty thin meal even though few people would know about it, but learning that the local small town pastor has&quot;exclusive&quot; relationships with several different members of his congregation on the sly could be potentially quite rewarding, even without the threat of revealing it.<br /> <br /> I could see the Hunger for Change as well that others have mentioned working well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T08:30:40-07:00","id":859025,"title":"","content":"I was briefly working on an idea for a &quot;Wendigo&quot; family of Hunger for Hunger, wherein it was Beasts that fed on Beasts and took their sustenance from undermining or appropriating the Hungers of other Beasts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The phrase 'flies on the heads of pins' appeared 43 times in that journal, sometimes in the middle of sentences or written in the margins.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4871-malkydel","name":"Malkydel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4871_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T10:57:58-07:00","id":859119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/858600-missing-families-hungers?p=858953#post858953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Hunger for Pleasure is one that I would really like to see. If it doesn't make it into the Player's Guide, I might just have to homebrew it. While I can see some overlap with some of the others that GibberingEloquence mentioned, I can also see some overlap between the existing Hungers, as well. The key difference that I'd see is that seeking excess might not be directly harmful by default, nor would it necessarily mean taking something from someone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hunger for Pleasure/Excess is the only one, so far, that strikes me as new territory. I'd favour Excess as a name, and lend it a self-destructive edge, as well as a vibe of things being used up. You FEAST NOW! at the risk of going hungry later. Or at the risk of everyone going hungry later (you might say it relates to Hoard the way Ruin relates to Prey).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would like to see a Hunger for Secrets as well. I see this as different from the Hoard in that a secret doesn't need to be taken from someone else necessarily. I'd imagine that the power of a secret, and thus how satisfying it would be to the Horror, would depend both on the obscurity of the knowledge gained and its potential effect should it be revealed. </div> </div> </div>Secrets seem like Power to me more than Hoard, but they also seem like a subset of Power full stop.<br /> <br /> Re Families...<br /> <br /> Put simply (and simplistically), Namtaru are scary because they're gross and wrong, Anakim are scary because they're unstoppable, Eshmaki are scary because they're behind you right now, Ugallu are scary because they can take you at any moment, and Makara are scary because their environment is inimical and impenetrable. What else is there?<br /> <br /> Is there room for a dedicated scary-because-it's-seductive Family? Personally, I think no, that's covered by the &quot;treasures of the deep tempting you to dive in&quot; aspect of the Makara.<br /> <br /> &quot;Scary because you see yourself in it&quot; shoud go for all Beasts or none, not a specific Family.<br /> <br /> Scary because it's everywhere? Taking after the notion of malignant places, with the Horror and Lair (or at least the Heart) conflated more than other Beasts? Has potential, but would maybe need too much unique mechanical adjustment.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T11:39:09-07:00","id":859142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/858600-missing-families-hungers?p=858851#post858851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I went through a few lists of fears in search of something new. It's harder than I expected. A lot of fears could be covered by existing Families/Hungers, if you consider their implications broadly. That's why, even if we fail to find anything new, a few paragraphs in the Player's Guide to broaden these concepts wouldn't hurt. Most notably:<br /> <br /> Deceit/Revelation. As of now, the description of Makara focuses on aquatic themes. This makes them stand out among other families, who are often closer to ideas that environments. However, the general feeling I get from the Forums is that they are THE family for all the deceptive or enticing monsters (like Gumiho or Succubi), regardless of surroundings. The fear would stem from the revelation that you made bad choices or put your guard down and played along to your doom. If Makara need to focus on aquatic themes, this could be basis for another Family.<br /> <br /> Actually, lies and deceit could be basis for another Hunger.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, the Makara do seem to cover a whole lot of monster types. The aquatic imagery is closer to drowning or choking imagery, though. The Lairs of the Makara can be scorching deserts and radioactive wastelands just as easily as oceans, caves and dark jungles.<br /> <br /> I'd like more clarification on the purview and fitting concepts of each Family and Hunger. I personally had quite a bit of trouble getting the gist of the Eshmaki.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-04-2016, 02:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T14:12:25-07:00","id":859246,"title":"","content":"So, a couple things that I've kicked around my brainpan recently:<br /> <br /> <b>Nightmares of the Other</b> \u2013 These would include notions from spirit possession (think <i>The Exorcist</i>) to extreme parasitism (it was the thought of a sentient 'vanishing twin' level of parasite that inspired this, actually). Examples include terrors such as the 'cinematic version' of schizophrenia/ split personality (not the REAL condition, though), a malevolent malignancy growing inside like a thinking and hungry cancer, something akin to gaining (or BECOMING) the <b><a href=\"http://theoatmeal.com/comics/angler\" target=\"_blank\">parasitic male angler fish</a></b>, and even the idea of existing only as a puppet dancing on another's strings. I can see it having a really nice synergy with the characters from <b>Changeling: the Lost</b> as it includes a loss of agency, but it more has a vibe \u2013 to me, at least \u2013 of that feeling of being or having a stranger in one's own skin, offering interesting resonance to <b>Promethean: the Created</b> and also with the Unchained of <b>Demon: the Descent</b>, though the latter are far removed from the Primordial Dream... or are they? Note that, yeah, these nightmares COULD be covered by a Namtaru to some degree, but I believe that this is distinct enough to make it a family of its own. That's beyond the fact that these Horrors give me the willies like few other things can!<br /> <br /> <b>Nightmares of Loss</b> \u2013 These are the fears of atrophy, of the powerlessness that comes from forgetting or being forgotten, the terror we feel at the notion of part of what's always been 'myself' is gone forever. Different from the Makara who take ALL of you, this family chooses bite-sized portions that are vital to one's self-image. That loss of voice when needed, the certainty that your job has been eliminated in the new merger, even your dread of your daughter's wedding because you'll never be her daddy again, all of these are Horrors waiting in the Primordial Dream...<br /> <br /> <b>Edit</b>: Both of the above are expressions of the fear of extinction, which while it covers death, also includes those notions of what it is that makes each of us an individual. Extinction as expressed by the Makara is, frankly, the most extreme of this form of fear. The 'nightmares' above COULD be expressed by a Makara Horror, but I like the idea of a more granular approach. Alternately, you might wanna look into the introduction of a 'Z axis' to the game (a la changeling kiths, vampire bloodlines, etc.)? I dunno... I just love this game so much that I can't get it out of my head. Fear is actually THAT important to me, it turns out. Yeah, and THAT is why I'm playing these games. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":409,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","user":"Phaolan","date":". 04-04-2016, 05:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T18:34:22-07:00","id":859370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/858600-missing-families-hungers?p=859119#post859119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hunger for Pleasure/Excess is the only one, so far, that strikes me as new territory. I'd favour Excess as a name, and lend it a self-destructive edge, as well as a vibe of things being used up. You FEAST NOW! at the risk of going hungry later. Or at the risk of everyone going hungry later (you might say it relates to Hoard the way Ruin relates to Prey).<br /> <br /> Secrets seem like Power to me more than Hoard, but they also seem like a subset of Power full stop.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that Excess would be a better name than Pleasure, and if I end up homebrewing it, that is what I'd call it.<br /> <br /> I disagree that secrets are just a subset of the Hunger for Power, though. Not that Tyrants couldn't feed on secrets. I fully acknowledge that those could be quite effective for them, especially for blackmail purposes. I just think that there are other sides to it as well. The name that could be used to summon an infernal demon could easily be an important secret, for instance. I'm imagining a sphinx-like Horror that is always looking for new riddles, or a hag-like Horror that desires occult knowledge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T00:22:00-07:00","id":859511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baroqo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/858600-missing-families-hungers?p=858608#post858608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about a <b>&quot;fear of self&quot; </b>family?<br /> <br /> Makaras could do for it, but i think that - expanded enough - they could make a nice addition.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That would be good for a family who did not voluntarily choose to become Beasts. Prompting legends of those who were cursed by malefic forces.<br /> <br /> Their Heroes could be under the impression that they are putting the Beast out of its misery, and thus doing a good deed in the process.<br /> <br /> Not sure how you would convey that fear to others thought. Maybe give them some form of shape shifting power so they can impersonate their victims?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-05-2016, 03:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T12:14:40-07:00","id":859804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phaolan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/858600-missing-families-hungers?p=859246#post859246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Nightmares of Loss</b> \u2013 These are the fears of atrophy, of the powerlessness that comes from forgetting or being forgotten, the terror we feel at the notion of part of what's always been 'myself' is gone forever. Different from the Makara who take ALL of you, this family chooses bite-sized portions that are vital to one's self-image. That loss of voice when needed, the certainty that your job has been eliminated in the new merger, even your dread of your daughter's wedding because you'll never be her daddy again, all of these are Horrors waiting in the Primordial Dream...<br /> <br /> <b>Edit</b>: Both of the above are expressions of the fear of extinction, which while it covers death, also includes those notions of what it is that makes each of us an individual. Extinction as expressed by the Makara is, frankly, the most extreme of this form of fear. The 'nightmares' above COULD be expressed by a Makara Horror, but I like the idea of a more granular approach. Alternately, you might wanna look into the introduction of a 'Z axis' to the game (a la changeling kiths, vampire bloodlines, etc.)? I dunno... I just love this game so much that I can't get it out of my head. Fear is actually THAT important to me, it turns out. Yeah, and THAT is why I'm playing these games. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>A Z-axis could be an interesting addition to the game, but I'd like to see it composed of subsets of both Families and Hungers.<br /> <br /> The Nightmares of Loss could be an interesting Family, although I think that I'd expand it to the Nightmares of Sorrow. That would include loss and all the great examples you gave, of course, but it could also include regret for things that one has personally done or created. Think of a Beast version of Victor Frankenstein, where the Horror is spawned from his own short-sighted ambitions and the horrific consequences that followed. It is also the fear of what might yet be, a fear of how far one could fall, or a fear of the grief caused by having a loved one torn away unexpectedly. I think this could have a lot of potential.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","user":"White Oak Dragon","date":". 04-05-2016, 03:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T14:25:59-07:00","id":859874,"title":"","content":"The only thing I really feel is missing is a un-Family for orphans and others who don't fit in. Could easily be a fear of the unknown type family.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T14:54:34-07:00","id":859898,"title":"","content":"For centuries there Always were stories of monsters that tempt and manipulate you into breaking your moral code or other oaths,not just Demons,the Beast who tempts,manipulates or tricks you to give in to your darkest desires,not necessarily do to Evil but to do something <i>other,</i>the Beast that whispers in your ear and gives you the rope because it's more fun than Hanging you.<br /> Hunger for Malice!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 04-05-2016, 06:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T04:30:23-07:00","id":860223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/858600-missing-families-hungers?p=859370#post859370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree that secrets are just a subset of the Hunger for Power, though. Not that Tyrants couldn't feed on secrets. I fully acknowledge that those could be quite effective for them, especially for blackmail purposes. I just think that there are other sides to it as well. The name that could be used to summon an infernal demon could easily be an important secret, for instance. I'm imagining a sphinx-like Horror that is always looking for new riddles, or a hag-like Horror that desires occult knowledge.</div> </div> </div> </div>You make a good case.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T05:33:40-07:00","id":860246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/858600-missing-families-hungers?p=860223#post860223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You make a good case.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Where's the fear though? The scary thing about secrets isn't the secret itself but the power it holds. A demon's secret name isn't scary in and of itself. It's the threat that the demon could be summoned that inspires that fear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T07:22:52-07:00","id":860289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/858600-missing-families-hungers?p=860246#post860246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where's the fear though? The scary thing about secrets isn't the secret itself but the power it holds. A demon's secret name isn't scary in and of itself. It's the threat that the demon could be summoned that inspires that fear.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You make a good point there. Where is the fear? To expand on that question, does someone need to experience that fear for a Horror to get any satisfaction? Is possessing the demon's name enough because the Horror knows the potential danger that it has at its disposal, or does it take a human knowing that the Beast has such a thing and worrying what is going to happen with it? I guess we'd need to look at some of the other Hungers to compare. If we look at the Collectors, we can see that, in general, the moment of shock comes when a person realizes that they've lost something precious to them. The Hoard needs to be something that someone else would value, either in itself or what it represents. Thus, you can have both the gold-hoarding dragon and the creepy tooth fairy as part of the same Hunger. The Collector description also mentions that some Beasts prefer to seek out ancient and forgotten treasures to claim for their own. Where would be the fear in this situation? What about the Collectors who collect less tangible things, such as the example of the Beast who collects lovers. Sure, the High Satiety feeding required that the man would be outraged by the Beast's seduction, but what would the Low Satiety version require for such a thing? What about a Collector of artwork that manages to steal a famous painting, but replaces it with a forgery so skillfully done that the theft will not be noticed for years? Does a Tyrant who gains power need to abuse it in order to feed? If the Tyrant feeds by gaining a promotion over a co-worker, is the Satiety potential lost if the co-worker's reaction to the news is to shrug and work harder?<br /> <br /> The point that I was getting at with all that is that not every feeding requires fear to be effective. It seems to be the potential of it that makes the feeding. The Collector's Hoard may be valuable because someone would want something they have, not because it necessarily belonged to a person originally. The long lost treasure works for feeding because there would be someone out there that would want their treasure, not because they necessarily know that the Beast has it. The Horror just wants something shiny that it has gained. Likewise, for secrets, I would say that it is not the use of a secret that makes it valuable, but the potential effects that it holds. A new riddle satisfies the sphinx because it makes the Horror feel smarter, and it knows that a juicy riddle may allow them to eat some poor bastard that isn't as clever as itself at some point in the future. A demon's name satisfies the hag because she could summon it, not because she is going to do so. The pastor's little indiscretions are satisfying because that secret could tear apart the social fabric of an entire congregation. Fear could easily be gained simply by leaving a hint that <i>someone </i>knows the secret somewhere in the world, if it is deemed truly necessary. Fear could also be gained through the lengths that one might go through in order to gain a new one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T14:36:07-07:00","id":866528,"title":"","content":"How about a family centered around the Fear of Chaos? The uncontrollable and sudden change of everything that one clings to for stability. Or maybe the Fear of Madness, both becoming unhinged and of those who are unpredictable in their thoughts and actions.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T14:45:07-07:00","id":866530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/858600-missing-families-hungers?p=866528#post866528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about a family centered around the Fear of Chaos? The uncontrollable and sudden change of everything that one clings to for stability. Or maybe the Fear of Madness, both becoming unhinged and of those who are unpredictable in their thoughts and actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Typhons for the Family of Chaos?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T14:48:09-07:00","id":866531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/858600-missing-families-hungers?p=866530#post866530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Typhons for the Family of Chaos?</div> </div> </div> </div>Works for me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T14:56:42-07:00","id":866534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/858600-missing-families-hungers?p=866531#post866531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Works for me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm thinking that their symbol could be a number (7? 10?) reptilian heads on long necks, spiralling outwards from the centre. They would tend towards fluid or changeable forms which can alter at a moment's notice. <br /> I think that their Birthright could perhaps allow them to change one thing in their immediate environment. Like, they could change a locked door to be unlocked or they could change the door to water. They couldn't affect living things though. <br /> I think that as well as the generic 'chaos', they would also be suited to the fear of uncertainty, of the future, of progress and so on.<br /> Sound OK?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T14:57:48-07:00","id":866535,"title":"","content":"Or perhaps they can alter the layout of their Lair more easily than other Beasts, changing Burrows around even as his enemies penetrate the Lair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T15:24:21-07:00","id":866539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/858600-missing-families-hungers?p=866534#post866534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that their Birthright could perhaps allow them to change one thing in their immediate environment. Like, they could change a locked door to be unlocked or they could change the door to water. They couldn't affect living things though. <br /> I think that as well as the generic 'chaos', they would also be suited to the fear of uncertainty, of the future, of progress and so on.<br /> Sound OK?</div> </div> </div> </div>Tying into the uncertainty thing and keeping it from being too powerful, maybe make it so it has to be a mundane change and it has to be in regards to something not been established in the scene, ala the Changeling power Hidden Reality?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T15:26:45-07:00","id":866543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/858600-missing-families-hungers?p=866539#post866539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tying into the uncertainty thing and keeping it from being too powerful, maybe make it so it has to be a mundane change and it has to be in regards to something not been established in the scene, ala the Changeling power Hidden Reality?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably better. I admit that when thinking of that I was thinking of Lovecraftian physics-bending monstrosities. Like a shoggoth with superpowers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T15:33:16-07:00","id":866546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/858600-missing-families-hungers?p=866539#post866539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tying into the uncertainty thing and keeping it from being too powerful, maybe make it so it has to be a mundane change and it has to be in regards to something not been established in the scene, ala the Changeling power Hidden Reality?</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is though, the fear I was thinking about is the kind where you think you have a solid footing, that everything makes sense, and then the rug is pulled from under you and everything's uncertain. You don't get that kind of shock if you never notice the change, or even know that the change occurred. Perhaps it could be the other way around, as in you can only change what is confirmed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T16:00:37-07:00","id":866552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/858600-missing-families-hungers?p=866528#post866528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about a family centered around the Fear of Chaos? The uncontrollable and sudden change of everything that one clings to for stability. Or maybe the Fear of Madness, both becoming unhinged and of those who are unpredictable in their thoughts and actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>This remember a my past idea.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Throne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/858600-missing-families-hungers?p=858857#post858857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hunger of Twist?<br /> The idea is based upon the character of Joker (Nolan version).<br /> The beast seek to scramble the life of the victim up down.<br /> It is not simply prey or collector (it must not &quot;tag&quot; a victim or stole/harm, anyting), or Nemesis (a routine is not a &quot;wrong&quot; about nobody, per se), neither ruin (the subject is a single person and the change is not only about &quot;damage&quot;).</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T02:56:11-07:00","id":866738,"title":"","content":"For the Family of Chaos, what do you think would be their name for the Dark Mother, ala the First Woman, She Who Lives In Her Shadow etc? So far, the best I've got is She of the Infinite Faces.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T03:05:20-07:00","id":866740,"title":"","content":"I've had a go at starting a write-up of the Typhons. If anyone wants to help, here's a link to the GDoc that allows editing. Please don't mess it up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1f4e_2V7PqfCUJKEvikpoLLsPBfy0Udg9M83z1HQuW5s/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=